  "title": "Explore primary clustering with linear probing and character-sum hashing",
  "explanation": "Introduce a custom linear-probing table with one-slot steps and wraparound. Change the hash function to an order-insensitive character sum, a different poor hash that concentrates ordinary text in a narrow range. Reserve about 20 percent empty slots so construction always terminates. This tests how a weak hash creates long primary clusters under open addressing, rather than linked chains. Every occupied probe counts, including repeated-key records.",
